---
/**
 * ABOUT BRANDURE — the agency first, the founder second.
 *
 * This page used to open on "Joe Hickman", so the first thing an engine read
 * on the page named to answer "what is Brandure" was a person. The answer-
 * first opening fixed that in November; this rewrite finishes the job by
 * describing all three services rather than AEO alone, which is what the
 * rest of the site has sold since /services was built.
 *
 * THE FOUNDER STAYS. The visible section below, the Person node at
 * /about#person and Organization.founder are all unchanged in substance —
 * every research article's byline and Article author reference that @id, so
 * it is load-bearing, not decoration.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

/* The Person node for @id https://brandure.io/about#person is NOT defined
   here. It lives in BaseLayout and is emitted sitewide, so this page gets it
   like every other page. Re-adding it here would resolve that @id to two
   full nodes, which is the duplication that consolidation removed. */
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Brandure: AEO, SEO and web design agency, UK & UAE"
  fullTitle
  description="Brandure is a remote AEO, SEO and web design agency serving the UK and UAE, getting businesses named in ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews and Perplexity."
>
  <section class="hero hero--short">
    <div class="mesh" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="mesh__layer mesh__layer--1"><div class="mesh__blob mesh__blob--1"></div></div>
      <div class="mesh__layer mesh__layer--2"><div class="mesh__blob mesh__blob--2"></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap res-hero" data-load>
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="statement" data-split>About Brandure</h1>
      {/* THE ENTITY LINE, as high on the page as it goes. It names the
          domain because the domain is what makes the entity unambiguous, and
          it states the three services and the two markets in one sentence an
          engine can lift whole. */}
      <p class="lede">
        Brandure (brandure.io) is a remote AEO, SEO and web design agency
        serving the UK and UAE.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow" data-reveal>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Brandure helps businesses get named and cited in the answers
          ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews and Perplexity give their buyers, and
          ranked on Google for the same questions. Every engagement starts by
          measuring where a business stands across those three engines, each
          one reported separately, then fixes the causes: website
          foundations, entity data, answer-ready content and the third-party
          sources the engines cite.
        </p>
        <p>
          We work remotely across the UK and the UAE. See{' '}
          <a href="/services">what we do</a>, <a href="/method">how we work</a>
          {' '}and <a href="/research">our research</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>AI search optimisation (AEO).</strong> Getting you named
            when buyers ask ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews and Perplexity who to
            use. Each engine is measured and reported separately, because the
            same business can be named in one and missing from another.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>SEO.</strong> Ranking on Google for the searches that
            bring buyers. Most of the groundwork overlaps with AI search, so
            it is included in every plan.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Web design.</strong> New pages or a full rebuild on the
            platform you already use, built so Google and AI assistants can
            read, trust and recommend you.{' '}
            <a href="/ai-ready-websites">How we build</a>.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* The founder section, kept. Its opening clause now describes the agency
      the same way the rest of the page does — it said "an answer engine
      optimisation agency" while every other line on the page said three
      services, and one of the two had to be wrong. */}
  <section class="section section--sunk">
    <div class="wrap-narrow" data-reveal>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Joe Hickman</h2>
        <p>
          Joe Hickman is the founder of Brandure, a remote AEO, SEO and web
          design agency serving the UK and UAE: how businesses get named in
          ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews and Perplexity, and found on Google.
        </p>
        <p>
          He has a background in paid social across Meta, Google, TikTok and
          LinkedIn.
        </p>
        <p>
          Brandure publishes its own measurement rather than citing other people&rsquo;s.{' '}
          <a href="/research">The research index</a> carries the questions asked, the
          market, the engines and the run count behind every figure.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="center-row mt-2">
        <a class="btn" href="/#report">Get a free visibility report</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
